.TH "LARGESTCONTENTFULPAINT.TOJSON" "3JS" "October 30, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
LargestContentfulPaint.toJSON \- LargestContentfulPaint: toJSON() method
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]toJSON()\f[B]\f[R] method of the
\f[CR]LargestContentfulPaint\f[R] interface returns a JSON\-serializable
plain object representing the \f[CR]LargestContentfulPaint\f[R] object.
.PP
The method is automatically called by \f[CR]JSON.stringify()\f[R] when a
\f[CR]LargestContentfulPaint\f[R] object is encountered during JSON
serialization.
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
toJSON()
.EE
.SS Parameters
None.
.SS Return value
A JSON\-serializable plain object containing the following properties:
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]name\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]entryType\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]startTime\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]duration\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]navigationId\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]paintTime\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]presentationTime\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]size\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]renderTime\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]loadTime\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]id\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]url\f[R]
.PP
Each property\(cqs value is copied as\-is.
.PP
The returned object doesn\(cqt contain the \f[CR]element\f[R] property
because \f[CR]Element\f[R] doesn\(cqt provide a \f[CR]toJSON()\f[R]
operation.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Calling toJSON() directly
This example obtains a \f[CR]LargestContentfulPaint\f[R] object.
Calling \f[CR]toJSON()\f[R] directly returns a plain object.
Its properties have the same values as the corresponding properties of
the original object.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] observer = \f[B]new\f[R] PerformanceObserver((list) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  list.getEntries().forEach((entry) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
    \f[B]const\f[R] json = entry.toJSON();
    console.log(json); \f[I]// A plain object\f[R]
    console.log(\f[B]typeof\f[R] json); \f[I]// \(dqobject\(dq\f[R]
    console.log(json.size); \f[I]// Same value as entry.size\f[R]
  });
});

observer.observe({ type: \(dqlargest\-contentful\-paint\(dq, buffered: \f[B]true\f[R] });
.EE
.SS Serializing to a JSON string
Within the callback from the previous example, the same object can be
serialized using \f[CR]JSON.stringify()\f[R], which calls the
\f[CR]toJSON()\f[R] method automatically.
.IP
.EX
console.log(JSON.stringify(entry));
.EE
.PP
This would log a JSON string like so (formatted for readability):
.IP
.EX
{
  \(dqname\(dq: \(dq\(dq,
  \(dqentryType\(dq: \(dqlargest\-contentful\-paint\(dq,
  \(dqstartTime\(dq: 468.5,
  \(dqduration\(dq: 0,
  \(dqnavigationId\(dq: 2463,
  \(dqpaintTime\(dq: 460.25,
  \(dqpresentationTime\(dq: 468.5,
  \(dqsize\(dq: 19824,
  \(dqrenderTime\(dq: 468.5,
  \(dqloadTime\(dq: 0,
  \(dqid\(dq: \(dq\(dq,
  \(dqurl\(dq: \(dq\(dq
}
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]JSON\f[R]
